d from tensile_data.csv.\nSpecimenTemp (C)Stress (MPa)Strain (%)A-1012545022.4A-10210042024.1B-20130031035.0C-50060012045.2","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/data/","title":"Automated Data Pipelines"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/gallery/":{"body":"\n    \n    \n        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n    \n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/gallery/","title":"High-Throughput Microscopy"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/molecules/":{"body":"We use 3Dmol.js to render protein structures.\nHemoglobin (4HHB)\nThe oxygen-transport metalloprotein in red blood cells.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Interaction: Left-Click Rotate | Scroll Zoom | Right-Click Pan\n\n\nInsulin (4INS)\nA peptide hormone produced by beta cells of the pancreatic islets.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Interaction: Left-Click Rotate | Scroll Zoom | Right-Click Pan\n\n\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/molecules/","title":"Molecular Dynamics Visualization"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-science/":{"body":"In Materials Science, we often write prototype simulations in Python and production codes in Fortran. Rust offers a third way.\n\n    Hypothesis\n    Rust can match the speed of Fortran while offering the package management of Python.\n\nThe Iterator Pattern\nConsider calculating the average energy of a lattice:\n\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-science/","title":"Zero-Cost Abstractions in Science"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-typst/":{"body":"Typst is a new markup-based typesetting system that is much faster than LaTeX.\nExample Embed\n\n    Typst Render\n    \n  F = ma\n\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-typst/","title":"Scientific Typesetting with Typst"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/this-is-blog-no2/":{"body":"Here is my first trial This is a trial to get to render a blog!\nExample Embed\n\n    Typst Render\n    \n  F = ma\n\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/this-is-blog-no2/","title":"Scientific Typesetting with Typst"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/typst/":{"body":"Mathematical Notation\nRendered via Typst:\n\n    \n    \n    Fig. Navier-Stokes Equation\n    \n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/typst/","title":"Scientific Typesetting"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/cv/":{"body":"About Voxel Space.\nMy work focuses on the deterministic simulation of stochastic physical processes. By moving scientific kernels from legacy Fortran/Python to Rust, we gain memory safety without sacrificing performance.\nTechnical Stack\nAreaTechnologies\nLanguagesRust, Python, C++, GLSL\nWebWebAssembly, Trunk, Zola, Tokio\nScienceMolecular Dynamics, Monte Carlo, DFT\nToolsGit, Docker, LaTeX, Blender\n\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/cv/","title":"About"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/":{"body":"Interactive WebAssembly Demos by Gokay.\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/","title":"Demos"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/grain-growth/":{"body":"Simulating the evolution of crystal grains in a metal during annealing.\n\n    \n        ACTIVE :: MICROSTRUCTURE EVOLUTION\n        \n            Open Fullscreen ↗\n        \n    \n    \n    \n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/grain-growth/","title":"Grain Growth"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/porosity-lab/":{"body":"This experiment simulates a porous microstructure and calculates accessible surface area.\n\n    \n        ACTIVE :: MICROSTRUCTURE ANALYZER\n        \n            Open Fullscreen ↗\n        \n    \n    \n    \n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/porosity-lab/","title":"Porosity Lab"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/":{"body":"Selected Works &amp; Experiments.\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/","title":"Projects"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/hpc/":{"body":"Status: Beta | Stack: Rust, Tokio, SQLite\nA \"Sergeant-Soldier\" orchestration system for managing thousands of concurrent molecular dynamics simulations across heterogeneous clusters.\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/hpc/","title":"Rust HPC Orchestrator"},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/porosity/":{"body":"Status: Active | Stack: Rust, Trunk, Web-Sys\nA zero-install, browser-based tool that calculates geometric porosity.\nLaunch Demo\n","id":"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/porosity/","title":"Porosity Lab (WASM)"}},"docInfo":{"http://127.0.0.1:1031/":{"body":33,"title":1},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/about/":{"body":41,"title":0},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/":{"body":0,"title":1},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/data/":{"body":12,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/gallery/":{"body":0,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/molecules/":{"body":40,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-science/":{"body":29,"title":4},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/rust-typst/":{"body":15,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/this-is-blog-no2/":{"body":12,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/blog/typst/":{"body":9,"title":2},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/cv/":{"body":41,"title":0},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/":{"body":4,"title":1},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/grain-growth/":{"body":12,"title":2},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/lab/porosity-lab/":{"body":13,"title":2},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/":{"body":4,"title":1},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/hpc/":{"body":18,"title":3},"http://127.0.0.1:1031/projects/porosity/":{"body":17,"title":3}},"length":17},"lang":"English"}